  "user_request_original": "Optimize the thicknesses of a 12-layer planar stack consisting of alternating HfO2 and SiO2 layers on a Silicon substrate with Air incidence at 0 degrees. Target high absorptance in 8000-13000 nm and low absorptance in 3000-5000 nm. Initialize thicknesses at 440 nm +/- 20 nm random perturbation. Enforce tighter thickness bounds on outer layers (indices 0, 1, 10, 11) to preserve entrance/exit interface impedance matching. Use Adam optimizer with reduced learning rate to dampen oscillatory thickness drift. Evaluate absorptance via Transfer Matrix Method. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 3000-5000 nm, 8000-13000 nm. soft objectives: high emissivity in 8000-13000 nm; low emissivity in 3000-5000 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high emissivity in 3000-5000 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layer count not exceeding 24.",
